WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.459
- I am my authentic self,

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:02.659
and I'm also the parent

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:05.537
my children need me to be for them.

00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.954
(soft music)

00:00:09.098 --> 00:00:11.399
We've been married for 13 years now.

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:14.978
- We've been together for 15 years.

00:00:14.978 --> 00:00:15.878
- We have two children,

00:00:15.878 --> 00:00:17.799
Jonathan and Jeanette,

00:00:17.799 --> 00:00:18.979
10 and eight years old.

00:00:18.979 --> 00:00:19.919
- We have three kids.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.119
So, we have four-year-old
twins and an eight-year-old.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.679
- Family means to me,

00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:25.879
my two dads and my brother.

00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:28.762
- Mama and Mo-pen and Bella.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.078
- We've actually been
married for two years,

00:00:30.078 --> 00:00:31.159
this will be year number three

00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:33.599
'cause we were just allowed to
get married a few years ago.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.119
- Before then, it was like,
we would call each other wife

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:37.499
and I would be waiting
for someone to be like,

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:39.518
"you can't do that"
which people would say.

00:00:39.518 --> 00:00:40.351
- Because at the beginning,

00:00:40.351 --> 00:00:41.617
we were kind of just making it up

00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:42.450
and then it was kinda like,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.456
yeah that's actually what it's called,

00:00:43.456 --> 00:00:45.896
we're actually married,
and she's my wife, yay.

00:00:45.896 --> 00:00:47.436
- Yay.

00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:49.436
- Family is at least two people

00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:51.356
who can rely upon each other.

00:00:51.356 --> 00:00:55.796
- Most people don't have
two dads or two moms.

00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:58.415
- No one in my class does.

00:00:58.415 --> 00:00:59.735
- What?

00:00:59.735 --> 00:01:00.912
- One of the things that I remember

00:01:00.912 --> 00:01:03.053
when we first had our children,

00:01:03.053 --> 00:01:04.413
was when we'd be out in public,

00:01:04.413 --> 00:01:05.832
the stares that we would get.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:09.152
- The struggle of, sort
of how people view you is,

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:10.372
it's a battle everyday.

00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:14.093
And funny enough, people will
really, like, in the elevator

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:16.412
ask you questions about
your family and your life.

00:01:16.412 --> 00:01:18.273
- I've also taught my children,

00:01:18.273 --> 00:01:21.294
not all questions come from a bad place,

00:01:21.294 --> 00:01:24.632
sometimes a person will ask a
question they just don't know

00:01:24.632 --> 00:01:26.032
and they want to know.

00:01:26.032 --> 00:01:29.115
- A family is a big sister or brother

00:01:30.732 --> 00:01:34.073
and a mommy or a daddy.
- [Boy] And a doggy.

00:01:34.073 --> 00:01:35.873
- They love us, they
want to take care of us

00:01:35.873 --> 00:01:37.853
and they want to be with us.

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:39.192
- I think in some circumstances

00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:40.292
they will have it harder in life,

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:42.532
but in other areas, I think
they're gonna be stronger.

00:01:42.532 --> 00:01:44.272
I mean, who better to parent you,

00:01:44.272 --> 00:01:47.352
than people who've had to
persevere their whole life.

00:01:47.352 --> 00:01:50.233
- For them, you know, what
they have is their norm,

00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:52.473
so I don't know that
they would say anything

00:01:52.473 --> 00:01:54.233
more different than any other kid.

00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:58.413
- I'm lucky to have my momma
and my M-O and my siblings.

00:01:58.413 --> 00:02:02.493
- We are crazy, we are dinner and a show.

00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:04.053
We're never boring.

00:02:04.053 --> 00:02:08.250
- Whenever we're at,
like, my friend's house,

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.650
my dad always like starts dancing

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.010
and he always makes everybody laugh.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.927
- DeSean, he wants to
always have, go shopping,

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.967
dress up and, always, he wants to have fun

00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:22.847
with me and Jonathan all the time.

00:02:22.847 --> 00:02:25.928
- My children will be prepared
to deal with the world,

00:02:25.928 --> 00:02:28.148
they'll be prepared to deal with people

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.847
who will embrace them
and they'll be prepared

00:02:29.847 --> 00:02:32.047
to deal with people
who won't embrace them.

00:02:32.047 --> 00:02:33.467
- You can get married, you can have kids,

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.527
you can have all these things.

00:02:34.527 --> 00:02:36.447
- It's the best feeling
in the whole wide world,

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:38.447
to have that experience.

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.847
- There's no one I would
rather parent with,

00:02:41.847 --> 00:02:45.407
especially as a gay
parent, other than Joel.

00:02:45.407 --> 00:02:47.824
(soft music)

00:02:50.743 --> 00:02:52.868
(swishing, squeaking)

